  "description": "Change of use at ground and basement level from A3 to auction sales room (sui generis) with associated retail (A1) and cafe/bar (A3/A4).",
  "site_name": "30-34",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "23/12/2010",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "W4 1TE",
  "street_name": "Chiswick High Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Other change of use",
  "lapsed_date": "22/12/2013",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans named Existing and Proposed Plans submitted on 27th October 2010 therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The use hereby permitted for A1, A3 and A4 uses ancillary to the principal sui generis use (auction sales) shall not be carried on outside the following times 7am to 8pm Mondays, Wednesdays and Thursdays; 8am to 8pm Saturdays; 10am to 6pm Sundays and Bank Holidays; 7am to 10pm Tuesdays; and 7am to 9.30pm Fridays.",
    "Condition : 4 - The A1, A3 and A4 uses shall be ancillary to the auction sales use hereby approved and shall occupy no more than 107m? of the floor area within the premises.",
    "Condition : 5 - The access doorway to No.30-34 Chiswick High Road shall have a minimum clear width of 900mm (1800mm for double doors), a level surface or ramp between the pavement and the floor and a door handle of not more than 1m above ground level.",
    "Condition : 6 - The disabled toilet shall be Disability Discrimination Act (DDA) compliant and a ramp shall be provided from the auction sales area to the platform area in the caf?/bar that is usable for wheelchair users.",
    "Condition : 7 - No deliveries and removal of any purchased items shall be taken at or despatched from the site outside the hours of 9am and 6pm nor at any time on Sundays, Bank or Public Holidays.",
    "Condition : 8 - The use of any PA and use of any system capable of playing amplified music, is controlled such that the volume is inaudible when assessed from the site boundary with the closest residential premises.  The use of any amplified system is restricted to Tuesday auctions only, and can operate no later than 10pm.  No amplification system shall be used and no amplified music shall be played on any other day.",
    "Condition : 9 - The proposal shall satisfy the requirements of the current Building Regulations (2010), with respect to Approved Document E 'resistance to the passage of sound', which concerns sound insulation."
  ],
